 "title": "Auditor / LaGrange County, Indiana",
 "text": "Auditor / LaGrange County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nLaGrange County, Indiana\nSearch\nSubmit\nMenu\nHome\nGovernment  Assessor\nAuditor\nBuilding\nCircuit Court\nClerk\nCoroner\nCommissioners\nCounty Council\nEmergency Management Agency\nGIS\nHealth\nHighway\nHuman Resources\nMaintenance\nParks\nPlanning & Zoning\nProbation\nProsecuting Attorney\nPublic Defender Office\nPurdue Extension\nRecorder\nSheriff\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSuperior Court\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nVeterans Service Office\nPay Property Tax  Tax Payments\nPrint Tax Bills\nCalendar\nNews & Notices\nHow Do I?  Browse the County Staff\nFind an Event\nFind a Location\nFind a Service\nSubmit a Request\nView FAQs\nView a Slideshow\nVisit the Meeting Center\nFind a Document  Agendas\nBreaking News\nForms & Applications\nMinutes\nNews & Notices\nUseful Links\nStart Content\nHome\nDepartments\nAuditor\nAuditor\nThe Auditor is the principal financial officer in county government and is defined under IC 36-2-9-2 as the fiscal officer of the county.\nThe Auditor serves as a secretary to the Board of County Commissioners and as clerk to the County Council.\nThe Auditor has responsibility for keeping accounts and issuing checks for the county. As a result, the Board of Commissioners, the County Council and other officials often look to the Auditor for day-to-day operational assistance, information and advice.\nIn keeping accounts and issuing warrants, the Auditor must develop financial analysis and cash flow projections and assist with budget preparations.\nThe county Auditor must also prepare and file an annual financial report with the State Board of Accounts.\nThe Auditor is directly responsible for preparing tax duplicates that show the value of property and taxes assessed against each taxpayer.\nAs a part of the tax function, the Auditor must also prepare plats that show the ownership and assessed valuation of each parcel in each township in the county. The plats much contain information prescribed by the Department of Local Government Finance and must be kept current.\nRecent News\nUseful Links\nForms\nRecent News\nLaGrange License Branch Relocation\nNotice of Elimination of Mortgage Deduction\nUseful Links\nDLGF Tax Bill Estimator\nGUTS - Tax Sale\nDepartment of Local Government Finance\nIndiana Transparency Portal\nForms\nHow to File for Deductions/Credits\nHomestead Deduction\nIndiana Property Tax Benefits - Overview\nContact Us\nKathryn Hopper ,\nAuditor\nCounty Office Building\n114 W Michigan St\nLaGrange, IN 46761 Get Directions\nBusiness: (260) 499-6310\nFax: (260) 499-6401\nStaff Directory\nHours: Monday - Friday\n8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.\nIn this Department\nProperty Tax Deductions\nPayroll\nAccounts Payable\nProperty Transfers\nJump to a division Make a Selection Property Tax Deductions Payroll Accounts Payable Property Transfers Section Home\nTopics of Interest\nIndiana Gateway - Public Information about local government\nJump to a topic or subtopic Make a Selection Indiana Gateway - Public Information about local government Topic Home\nMore Information\nFind content and services related to this page.\nDocument Center Forms & Applications\nNews & Notices\nUseful Links\nJump to a content archive Make a Selection Document Center\n- News & Notices\n- Useful Links\n- Forms & Applications\nCourthouse\n105 N Detroit St., LaGrange, IN 46761\n260-499-6300\nOffice Building\n114 W Michigan St., LaGrange, IN 46761\n260-499-6300\nJustice Building\n105 N High St., LaGrange, IN 46761\n260-499-6300\n© 2026 LaGrange County, Indiana\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use\nSite Design and Content Management by\nCORE Business Technologies",
